{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1456081-what-s-wrong-with-bringing-back-1e-psyche","id":1456081,"title":"What's wrong with bringing back 1e Psyche?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Geist: The Sin-Eaters"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-08-03T11:06:38-07:00","id":1456081,"title":"What's wrong with bringing back 1e Psyche?","content":"I haven't played first edition Geist but I know there used to be Psyche as a Supernatural Tolerance trait separate from the Morality Trait, Synergy.<br /> <br /> I understand <i>why </i>they merged the two traits into a single one in 2nd edition. With Synergy as a measure of both a Sin-Eater power and how well aligned he is with his Geist, not only it makes sense to have the two correlated, but it also shifts the game's focus more on Remembrance and resolving the Geist's Burden.<br /> <br /> However, I am wondering if there are any actual drawbacks or problems with separating the Supernatural Tolerance trait from Synergy (Psyche or whatever you want to call it).<br /> <br /> From a strictly ST point of view, I find it easier when the splats are more similar to each other and more streamlined.<br /> From a player's point of view, while I played to 2e Geist, it felt weird that the game <i>forced </i>me to follow more personal stories, thus deviating from the chronicle's main plotline, in order to raise my Supernatural Tolerance trait (while in other games it's usually just a 5xp cost).<br /> <br /> So, other than changing the Theme and Story focus of the game, what would be wrong with bringing back Psyche?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26440-moonwhisper","name":"moonwhisper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26440_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-03T17:50:14-07:00","id":1456094,"title":"","content":"Setting aside the thematics, which you acknowledged, the primary issue I see is in the amount of work needed, mechanically, to hack them apart in the system. <br /> <br /> All the rolls and benefits which utilize Synergy currently would have to be divided between Power Stat and Integrity. Costs for raising each would need to be redefined, as well as the free increase conditions\u2026<br /> <br /> And in looking at that list of mechanics, I\u2019m starting to wonder \u201cwhat\u2019s left for the synergy (relationship) trait?\u201d What would actually be tied to it? What incentive would players have to raise it? Breaking points and\u2026?<br /> <br /> I think Synergy (the integrity version) will be a hobbled stat, though, and that the line between \u201csupernatural potency\u201d vs \u201crelationship with Geist\u201d will become difficult to draw, and the system redesigns for how to increase (or lose) either trait will be surprising complex.<br /> <br /> And you can already raise Synergy by just spending EXP, so\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-06T13:20:59-07:00","id":1456257,"title":"","content":"Yes, you can gain new synergy dots by spending 5 experience points as well.<br /> <br /> Of course I think increasing it by ivestigating your geist backstory or solving it's burdens is more rewarding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-09T06:58:02-07:00","id":1456426,"title":"","content":"Oh, nevermind then. The ST must have houseruled that in the game I played.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seraph Kitty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1456081-what-s-wrong-with-bringing-back-1e-psyche?p=1456094#post1456094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Synergy (the integrity version) will be a hobbled stat, though, and that the line between \u201csupernatural potency\u201d vs \u201crelationship with Geist\u201d will become difficult to draw, and the system redesigns for how to increase (or lose) either trait will be surprising complex.</div> </div> </div> </div>Makes sense. It *did* work out in 1st ed., but now it would too complex to split it for the scope of some house-ruling. One would have to basically redesign everything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26440-moonwhisper","name":"moonwhisper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26440_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}